<title>POLAND: Polish currency reserves rise to $18.03 bln in '96.</title>
<headline>Polish currency reserves rise to $18.03 bln in '96.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish official foreign currency reserves, those held by the central bank alone, grew by $3.07 billion in 1996 to $18.03 billion, the National Bank of Poland said.  </p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dollars)    DEC 96     DEC 95    DEC 94</p>
<p>    Official reserves		    18.03	 14.96	6.03</p>
<p>    Net reserves			   21.81	 20.44     11.30</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
